Experiment 36: Open Chrome Browser Using Selenium WebDriver and Verify the Title of ARMS Portal

# AIM
To open the Chrome browser using Selenium WebDriver, navigate to the ARMS portal and verify the page title.

# ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Import the required Selenium WebDriver packages.
3. Create an instance of ChromeDriver.
4. Open the Chrome browser.
5. Navigate to the ARMS portal URL.
6. Get the page title using the `getTitle()` method.
7. Verify the title using the `assertEquals()` method.
8. Close the browser.
9. Stop the program.

# CODE

**File: ARMSPortalTitleTest.java**

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class ARMSPortalTitleTest {

    @Test
    public void verifyARMSPortalTitle() {

        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.get("https://arms.srmist.edu.in/");

            String actualTitle = driver.getTitle();

            System.out.println("Page Title: " + actualTitle);

            assertEquals("ARMS", actualTitle);

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}
```

